  "goodToKnow": "Das Eigenkapital is equity or one's own capital, as opposed to das Fremdkapital (borrowed money). For a mortgage, German banks usually expect buyers to bring Eigenkapital of about 20 percent plus the purchase costs, which is one reason home ownership in Germany is low compared with other EU countries. Banks must hold minimum Eigenkapital under Basel rules. It has no plural."
